  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed rear L-shaped roof extension, by reason of its excessive width, height, depth and overall massing, would form a continuous and bulky roof addition and fail to appear as a subordinate addition to the host dwelling. The proposal would therefore result in harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the wider roofscape and surrounding area, contrary to Policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 of the Local Plan.\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would fail to provide a sufficient standard of accommodation for future occupiers by sub-standard internal space standard, communal and private amenity space. The proposal is therefore contrary to Local Plan policies SC5.\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal development fails to demonstrate that it would comply with the relevant sustainability requirements and result in sufficient carbon reductions on site. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan policies EQ1 and EQ2 and London Plan policy SI2.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development, by reason of the constrained size and layout of the site, would result in an unsatisfactory and unsafe arrangement of car parking, pedestrian access, cycle parking and refuse storage. The retention of off-street parking would significantly reduce the space available for essential servicing facilities, resulting in a cramped site layout and potential conflict between pedestrian and vehicular movements. As such, the proposal is contrary to London Plan Policy T6.1, Local Plan Policy EC2 and the Council's adopted Residential Crossover and Off-Street Parking Policy."
  ],
